cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cameleer in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Cameleer: Apache Camel's integration model in Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sudheesh
    family-names: PM
repository-code: "https://github.com/pmsudhi/cameleer"
url: "https://pmsudhi.github.io/cameleer/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-05"
keywords:
  - rust
  - apache-camel
  - enterprise-integration-patterns
  - integration
  - ai-agents
  - serverless
abstract: >-
  Cameleer is an independent reimplementation of Apache Camel in Rust: routes,
  Enterprise Integration Patterns, about 230 components, languages and data formats, and
  the Rust, YAML and XML DSLs, built on the Rust standard library only. It starts in about
  10 ms, uses about 10 MB of memory and outperforms Apache Camel on the JVM in published
  benchmarks.
references:
